# Ayli, Eternal Pilgrim: "{1}{W}{B}, Sacrifice another creature: Exile target nonland permanent. Activate only if you have at least 10
# life more than your starting life total" (CR 602.5). Bot1 starts at 28 life with Ayli, three Memnites, Mox Pearl, Mox Jet and a
# Black Lotus; on turn 3 it adds a Mox Ruby and taps the Lotus for WWW, Jet for B and Ruby for R (generic costs are paid from W first).
# The exile ability is refused at 28 and at 29 with the mana, a Memnite and a target all there; the first ability ("{1}, Sacrifice
# another creature: You gain life equal to the sacrificed creature's toughness") takes it from 28 to 29 and then 30, and at exactly 10
# above the starting 20 the exile ability exiles Bot2's Memnite (its Island is refused). It does not matter what the life total
# does afterwards (it is 30 still). On turn 5 it exiles Bot1's own Mox Pearl, paying {1}{W}{B} and sacrificing a Memnite.

